status GREEN -- rishi_run_record GREEN on metal in both roster passes, scan verdict=ok at claims_unknown_field=0, control 31 of 31 with faults=0; reds_ledger_monotone and reds_ledger_headline GREEN after the census move; the four repaired pages grade A, A and B+ under qa_report_card. HONEST GAP: both passes read one red that is not mine, standing_equipment's own control leg live_group_plant, which peers have booked since 20260907 (%549). AGAINST MYSELF: I moved the ledger headline while the first hot pass was running, so it closed tree_moved=yes and its receipt is withheld; the second pass held still and reads 161 guards, 1,242s, 158 green, 1 red, 2 gated, tree_moved=no.
recommend keep-going -- the same press applied to the two tongues still unread: TAME Core states Brix reflexes (every field bounded, override by double-seat rather than silent reflow) and Bron/Kyri reflexes (one key value per line, no quotes or braces, parsed rather than evaluated) in the same imperative, and nothing in this lap touched either. The question worth Keaton's word is one room over: the guard reads law pages for claims about ONE builtin's record, and Rishi has other builtins whose shapes are stated in prose the same way -- should the reading widen to every record the language returns, or stay narrow where the fault actually fired?
